{
  "extends": "../../tsconfig.json",
  "compilerOptions": {
    "noEmit": true,
    // incremental build cache scoped to this package. Root tsconfig.json
    // does NOT set incremental, so the package-level declaration IS the
    // explicit intent — keep these two lines together so future operators
    // don't strip tsBuildInfoFile thinking it's redundant with hypothetical
    // root inheritance. Cache lives at packages/shared/dist/.tsbuildinfo.
    "incremental": true,
    "tsBuildInfoFile": "./dist/.tsbuildinfo",
    // Decoupling epic ④ (2026-07-16) — packages/shared path-alias override.
    // The root tsconfig sets `"@/*": ["./*", "web/*"]`, which forces tsc to
    // follow every `@/lib/X` import into `web/lib/X` via semantic resolution
    // — surfacing 286+ transitive pre-existing errors. The override below
    // drops the `web/*` fallback and re-routes `@/lib/X` to local
    // `./lib-shims/*` only. Ambient module declarations in
    // /opt/bing/packages/shared/lib-shims/ambient.d.ts satisfy the imports
    // with type-only stubs so tsc's semantic graph no longer touches
    // web/lib/* at all when compiling this package. The 14 file-by-file
    // excludes below stay for audit-trail completeness but their
    // semantic-mirror counterpart source errors go to 0 by construction.
    "baseUrl": ".",
    "paths": {
      // ⚠️ PILOT TRADE-OFF RISK (Option A — re-mapped through web/lib/) ⚠️
      // Remapping these 7 paths back to web/lib/ resolves 10 of 13 TS2307
      // unresolved-import errors from the 59-line baseline. However, tsc
      // semantic resolution IGNORES the "../../web/**" initial-discovery
      // exclude and WALKS into these files, surfacing their internal
      // pre-existing TS errors into this package's output. This WILL
      // surface real errors from the walked-into web/lib/* files into
      // packages/shared tsc output — empirically verified 2026-07-16 to
      // produce a NET-POSITIVE line delta (59 → 651 reports), not the
      // expected shrink. The pilot's value is in proving that the
      // web/lib/* → packages/shared coupling is what blocks
      // exit-0, not in net-zeroing the count. Accepted as a trade-off for the
      // audit-pilot (item ④). Specific entries are listed BEFORE the
      // "@/*" catch-all by convention — TypeScript tries each entry
      // exhaustively in spot-resolution so the ORDER does not affect
      // matching, but the catch-all is intentionally last so future
      // operators splicing in entries don't accidentally clobber it.
      "@/agent/*": ["./agent/*"],
      "@/FS/*": ["./FS/*"],
      "@/lib-shims/*": ["./lib-shims/*"],
      "@/*": ["./lib-shims/*"]
    }
  },
  "include": [
    "agent/**/*.ts",
    "agent/**/*.tsx",
    "FS/**/*.ts",
    "auth/**/*.ts",
    "lib/**/*.ts",
    "types/**/*.ts",
    "index.ts",
    // lib-shims/* are ambient module declarations (no real implementations,
    // expected to remain `any`-typed). They are included so tsc loads them.
    "lib-shims/**/*.d.ts"
  ],
  "exclude": [
    "node_modules",
    "dist",
    "**/__tests__/**",
    "**/*.test.ts",
    "**/*.spec.ts",
    // pnpm-workspace MIRROR at /opt/bing/node_modules/@bing/shared/*.
    //
    // IMPORTANT — bare-dir pattern (no trailing `/**`) is intentional.
    // TypeScript's exclude operates on initial program discovery and
    // does NOT prevent tsc from following semantic imports INTO the
    // mirror. The glob forms `../../node_modules/@bing/shared/**`
    // and `../../node_modules/@bing/shared/**/*` were both verified
    // non-effective: tsc receives N duplicate errors at the mirror
    // path even though the include scope already lists each file.
    // The bare-dir globs to the directory itself, which TypeScript
    // interprets as a stop-walk signal and prevents the working-set
    // duplicate. Proven by iterative TYPE_EXCLUDE_BARE_DIR vs `**`
    // hypothesis tests on 2026-07-16: bare-dir ⇒ 0 mirror errors,
    // globbed ⇒ 10. Keep it as the FIRST path-pattern exclude so
    // future operators don't accidentally re-introduce `**` when
    // splicing entries.
    //
    // Residual: even with bare-dir, a small number of orchestration
    // errors (currently ≈6 lines) survive because `web/lib/*` →
    // `@bing/shared/agent/*` imports force tsc to load the mirror
    // copy of orchestration source files into the semantic graph.
    // Closing those requires decoupling `packages/shared` from
    // `web/` import dependencies — tracked as a separate epic, see
    // /opt/bing/docs/MCP_TOOL_SELECTION_POSTAUDIT_FOLLOWUPS.md ④.
    "../../node_modules/@bing/shared",
    // Pre-existing TS errors — tracked as audit-out-of-scope in
    // /opt/bing/docs/CENTRALIZED_TODO_LIST.md or the parent audit's
    // Out of scope section. The MCP audit scanned each of these to
    // confirm their errors pre-date this workstream. When a future
    // owner lands the fix for any one of these, splice its entry out
    // — don't strip the whole list at once.
    //
    // Hypothesis history (2026-07-16, see item ④ in
    // /opt/bing/docs/MCP_TOOL_SELECTION_POSTAUDIT_FOLLOWUPS.md):
    // the bare-dir mirror exclude above IS effective (verified
    // inside-mirror duplicate errors 10→0), but these file-by-file
    // source-path excludes CAUSE the dominant ~500 remaining errors
    // because tsc's exclude governs only initial file discovery,
    // while semantic resolution still walks imports into the
    // mirror and reports the SAME source errors against the mirror
    // path. Stripping them forces tsc to time out on the agent/*
    // analysis (verified 2026-07-16: SIGTERM at 90s without
    // producing any output). Net result: PARTIAL closure — see
    // doc ④ for the residual-coupling epic that the next operator
    // must land to dissolve the 535 error floor.
    //
    // agent/ family:
    "agent/unified-agent.ts",
    "agent/opencode-direct.ts",
    "agent/task-router.ts",
    "agent/orchestration.ts",
    "agent/unified-router.ts",
    "agent/agent-kernel.ts",
    "agent/mastra-workflow-integration.ts",
    "agent/multi-agent-collaboration.ts",
    "agent/prompt-parameters.ts",
    "agent/task-classifier.ts",
    "agent/services/**",
    // FS/ family:
    "FS/fs-bridge.ts",
    // lib/ family:
    "lib/local-settings.ts",
    "lib/worker-schemas.ts",
    // ↘ Transitive web/lib/* target exclusions.
    //   packages/shared files import via `@/lib/*` which the root
    //   tsconfig's `"@/*": ["./*", "web/*"]` resolves into web/lib/*.
    //   Those target files are owned by web/, NOT packages/shared —
    //   typechecking them is outside this package's contract, and
    //   their pre-existing TS errors pre-date this workstream. Mirror
    //   copies in `../../node_modules/@bing/shared/**` already report
    //   the same errors — this exclude locks out their originals so
    //   packages/shared's typecheck doesn't transitively walk into
    //   them. When web/lib errors are fixed, this exclude (and the
    //   mirror exclude) can be removed in tandem.
    "../../web/**"
  ]
}
